# 0006 - device-loss diagnostics: D3D12 DRED breadcrumbs + page faults (Gears 3 chat, 2026-10-23; base 27958a8)
# Why: Gears 3 lost the device TWICE tonight at the same spot (Act 1, CNV Sovereign, ~1 min after the SICKBAY
# corridor, ~6 min in): Gears2-Native play log gears3-20261023-002508 (0x887A0007) and Gears3-Native play log
# 20261023-004506 (0x887A0005), with 100-180 ms GPU frames in the ~20 s before. The log said nothing about why.
#   --gow2_gpu_dred=true  (gpu_system.cpp) EnableDeviceLossDiagnostics() before the provider creates the device:
#                         ID3D12DeviceRemovedExtendedDataSettings, breadcrumbs + page faults FORCED_ON (release runtime,
#                         Windows 10 1903+, no debug layer). Small GPU cost; false = as before.
#   D3D12Backend::IsLost -> ReportDeviceLoss() once: GetDeviceRemovedReason in words, every unfinished command list
#                         (done / total ops, the D3D12_AUTO_BREADCRUMB_OP numbers around the stop), the page-fault GPU
#                         VA with the live / recently freed allocations there (our textures already carry debug names).
#   The renderer's command list is named "gow2 renderer list".
# Checked: the new code compiles against current DirectX-Headers d3d12.h (SDL's copy) in a focused TU; Windows syntax
# check of gpu_system.cpp unchanged apart from known header noise. Not built or run. Independent of 0004 / 0005.
